    mir_result_type_erasure_blocks_execution_linked_error_contracts_2026-08-12, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: two findings. (1) The type-erasure half is already fixed at tip: MIR retains Result(ok, err) on constructor destinations and signatures (verified in serialized MIR), lower_result_construct_named emits typed rt_enum_new. (2) The doc's open interpreter-behavior arm reproduced: every typed Ok/Err construction, ? propagation and Result match failed E-INTERP-RUNTIME-Unknown no runtime owner for rt_enum_new (Runtime dispatch never consulted the caller-bound function table), and the ResultMatchSemantic witness arm returned a unit that the seed host coerced into a phantom Some(()) error aborting every executed Result match. Fix (src/compiler/95.interp/mir_interpreter.spl, +21/-1): _dispatch_call_operand Runtime case consults self._resolve_function(name) before the fixed native arity bridge (falls through unchanged when unbound); ResultMatchSemantic returns None. An FFI-bridged rt_enum_new attempt was tried and REVERTED (seed FFI returns high-level Value::Enum which poisons the tagged-word execution model). Spec test/01_unit/compiler/mir/result_linked_error_contract_execution_spec.spl 6/6 PASS (Result retention shape, executed Err + match payload, ?-chain propagation across functions, Ok payload extraction, early return Err, return f() of a linked call); neighbours result_predicates 8/0, result_payload_shape_gaps 12/0, result_tuple_unwrap 21/0, bare_result_return_spelled_guard 3/0, result_try_provider_tuple 10/0, result_native_integer_slot 3/0, result_try_record_array_workaround 5/0, folded_global_scalar_helper 3/0 all green. Side effect: optional_scalar_static_some_spec improved 8/10 to 15/3 (residual 3 pre-existing: one stale lowering-shape expectation, two model-scope gaps). Follow-up noted: case ScalableVecFence(_) has the same latent unit-return pattern off the Result path. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/mir/result_linked_error_contract_execution_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/mir/result_tuple_unwrap_spec.spl"

